meta {
  name: 04 Save QR Code Scan Settings
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-settings/qr-code-scan
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "billPrintablePaymentStatuses": ["PAID", "PARTIALLY_PAID"],
    "billPrintTemplateId": null,
    "reportPrintTemplateId": null
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("echoes back the saved settings", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d.billPrintablePaymentStatuses).to.have.members(["PAID", "PARTIALLY_PAID"]);
    expect(d.billPrintTemplateId).to.equal(null);
    expect(d.reportPrintTemplateId).to.equal(null);
  });
}

docs {
  Save (partial patch, upsert) the active branch's QR Code Scan settings. Every
  field is optional: a field left out keeps its current value; a template id sent
  as `null` clears the selection. The response is the resulting settings object.

  - `billPrintablePaymentStatuses` (string[]) — `PaymentStatus` names
    (`NOT_PAID` / `PARTIALLY_PAID` / `PAID`). Duplicates and unknown values are
    rejected with 400. Empty array = no bill printable.
  - `billPrintTemplateId` (string|null) — a `bill_print` template id in THIS
    tenant. A missing/other-tenant/wrong-type id is rejected
    (`QR_SCAN_TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND`, 422).
  - `reportPrintTemplateId` (string|null) — a `lab_all_report` template id in
    THIS tenant (same validation).

  Needs `branch_admin:branch_settings__update_branch_settings` (403 without it).
  Unknown fields, including `branchId`, are rejected with 400: the branch is always
  the caller's active branch from the JWT. Audited under
  `AuditModule.QR_CODE_SCAN_SETTINGS`.

  To list the templates for the two dropdowns:
  - Bill Print: `GET /pdf-report-templates?type=bill_print&status=ACTIVE`
  - Report Print: `GET /pdf-report-templates?type=lab_all_report&status=ACTIVE`
}
